{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":48900,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"ce95d1822fdf4e1aa6e2ccbd4d6bb8a7b0b16509dfe00ca40a918e997bfe4429","packTokens":19667,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":280,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":374,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":167,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":825,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":2369,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":1844,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":13695,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nAdversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.\nThis spec is for the web side of a product whose API is a separate service, built and tested from the same request in a run of its own. Behaviour listed out of scope citing API-SIDE is that run's work: don't flag it as missing, and don't flag a criterion for checking a server rule only through what the screen shows.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-12T19:22:21.823Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261012-meridian-coldchain-platform-in-9fcb\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"high\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"auth\",\n  \"payments\",\n  \"pii\",\n  \"migration\",\n  \"public-api\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [],\n \"touchesUi\": true\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users authenticate to the driver, staff, and customer areas?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use individual email-and-password accounts with self-service password reset.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can create, deactivate, and assign roles and access scopes to users, including a staff member’s warehouses and a customer user’s organisation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A System Administrator manages accounts, roles, warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"For a customer’s recall response, may reported on-hand, used/dispensed, and destroyed quantities total less than the quantity delivered, leaving a remainder unaccounted?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow a smaller total; track the remainder as unaccounted until it is later accounted for or written off with a signed justification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How long must the handover signature and delivery photo remain available?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain them for seven years, matching the audit-record retention period.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What existing records, if any, must be brought into the new system at launch so lot tracing and recall quantities work from the start?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Start with no imported records; enter opening lots and stock in the new app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who is authorized to sign a write-off of unaccounted recall quantities?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Manager.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"For a partial refusal, can the receiver refuse a quantity within a shipper box, or only accept/refuse whole boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record acceptance or refusal only for whole boxes, with a reason for each refused box.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What tier limits, allowance budgets, and permitted temperature ranges should drive excursion recommendations, and are they shared or product-specific?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use one configured set of tier limits and allowances for all products.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q5\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"US-010: Decide What Happens to Affected Stock\",\n   \"US-013: Audit Trail\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"When a new signed decision supersedes an earlier decision, should the new disposition automatically update the stock and its order/route state, including if it reverses the earlier disposition? → assumed: Apply the superseding decision to the stock and its order/route state, retaining the earlier decision and recording the resulting changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"reporting\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"US-014: Reports and Scheduled Summaries\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which period should the monthly report generated on the first day cover? → assumed: On-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q7\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"US-010: Decide What Happens to Affected Stock\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should the more-than-four-hour decision escalation reach the Quality Manager? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"US-011: Recall a Lot\",\n   \"US-014: Reports and Scheduled Summaries\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which email service should deliver recall notices, 24-hour reminders, daily summaries, and monthly reports? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"browsers\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"driver-route-loading-handover\",\n   \"US-012: Follow Orders in the Customer Portal\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which browsers and browser versions must support the responsive web app, including offline driver work and photo/signature capture? → assumed: The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"accessibility\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"driver-route-loading-handover\",\n   \"US-012: Follow Orders in the Customer Portal\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What accessibility conformance level is required for the web app and generated customer certificates? → assumed: WCAG 2.1 AA on the main flows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"volumes\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"US-011: Recall a Lot\",\n   \"US-014: Reports and Scheduled Summaries\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What launch scale should the app support, particularly for the recall trace that must be available within one minute? → assumed: Up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-10\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"If a route box is missing or a scanned box belongs to another route, can the driver complete loading and depart, or must the discrepancy be resolved first? → assumed: Block departure until every expected box is scanned and every wrong box is removed or corrected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-8\",\n   \"I-14\",\n   \"I-16\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"When a route changes while the driver is offline, how should unsent loading or refusal work that no longer matches the route be reconciled? → assumed: Keep the unsent work and require the driver to review differences and resolve affected boxes before continuing; preserve completed handovers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-14\",\n   \"I-16\",\n   \"I-41\",\n   \"I-46\",\n   \"I-47\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"If a recall is started while a driver is offline and the driver completes a handover before reconnecting, should that completed handover be retained as an exception or treated as blocked? → assumed: Retain the actual handover, flag the recall conflict, and open a quality case when it syncs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-12\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-11\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"If browser location access is denied or unavailable at handover, can the driver still complete the handover? → assumed: Allow completion and record that location was unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-21\",\n   \"I-42\",\n   \"I-50\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-12\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How will the existing logger and supplier gateway provide live temperatures, alert status, box association, and temperature history to the web app? → assumed: Use an existing gateway API or feed supplied by Meridian.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-25\",\n   \"I-33\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-13\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What identity check must a user repeat when signing a quality decision? → assumed: Confirm identity using whichever sign-in method the account uses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-37\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-14\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should a decision waiting more than four hours be escalated to the Quality Manager? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-16\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-41\",\n   \"I-50\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-15\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"For customers who have not responded within 24 hours of a recall notice, what reminder schedule and channel should be used? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-17\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-50\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-16\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which time zone should the customer portal use when the user's own time zone has not been set? → assumed: Use the time zone configured on the user's account.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"browsers\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-18\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-50\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-17\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which desktop and mobile browsers and versions must the responsive web app support? → assumed: The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"accessibility\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-19\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-50\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-18\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What accessibility conformance level is required for the web app? → assumed: WCAG 2.1 AA on the main flows.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-12T19:22:21.911Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261012-meridian-coldchain-platform-in-9fcb\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-5\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-6\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-7\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-8\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is ne