ld work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-46\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-47\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-48\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-49\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-50\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.\",\n  \"Launch scale is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.\",\n  \"Departure is blocked until every expected route box is scanned and wrong-route boxes are removed or corrected.\",\n  \"Unsent work affected by an offline route change remains available for review and resolution; completed handovers are preserved.\",\n  \"An offline handover completed despite a hold or recall conflict is retained, flagged, and associated with a quality case when synchronized.\",\n  \"Denied or unavailable browser location does not block a handover and is recorded as unavailable.\",\n  \"Live temperature, alert, box-association, and history data are supplied through an existing gateway API or feed.\",\n  \"A signer confirms identity using the sign-in method configured for that account.\",\n  \"Customer portal times use the user's configured account time zone.\",\n  \"Recall responses may leave a remainder unaccounted until later accounting or signed write-off.\",\n  \"Handover signatures and delivery photos are retained for seven years, matching audit-record retention.\",\n  \"A Quality Manager is authorized to sign a write-off.\",\n  \"Refusals are recorded by whole box, with a reason for each refused box.\",\n  \"One configured set of tier limits and allowances applies to all products.\",\n  \"Reports use on-screen date-range filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is included.\",\n  \"Quality-decision escalation and recall notices/reminders are email-only from fixed templates, with no SMS or push.\",\n  \"The customer portal and certificates support English and Arabic, including right-to-left Arabic layout.\",\n  \"The existing logger/gateway data and API/feed are supplied for consumption by the web app.\"\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"All pages render without horizontal scrolling at widths from 320 px through 1920 px; interactive touch targets on narrow viewports are at least 44 by 44 CSS px.\",\n   \"text\": \"The Meridian web app shall be responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"metric\": \"All primary driver and customer flows pass acceptance tests on the latest two released versions of each named browser.\",\n   \"text\": \"The Meridian web app shall support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"Automated accessibility checks report zero applicable WCAG 2.1 AA violations on main flows and manual keyboard checks pass.\",\n   \"text\": \"The main web-app flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"metric\": \"For responses containing up to 100,000 records, all returned trace entries are displayed or accessible within 60 seconds after the response is received.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web app shall render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n   \"metric\": \"With fixtures representing 1,000 users and 100,000 records, the trace screen displays the complete returned trace within 60 seconds of the user's request.\",\n   \"text\": \"The web client shall support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"API-side enforcement of credentials, password-reset token validity/delivery, role and access-scope authorization, and account state; web requirements cover forms, requests, screens, and API response handling.\",\n  \"API-side persistence and enforcement of stock/order/route transitions, hold and recall blocking across warehouses, quarantine, quantity validation/conservation, recall trace completeness and arithmetic, recall closure eligibility, write-off authorization, and duplicate-handover idempotency.\",\n  \"API-side audit creation, tamper detection, immutability, seven-year retention of audit records and handover evidence, and certificate-version persistence.\",\n  \"API-side scheduled and outbound emails, including recall notices and 24-hour reminders, four-hour decision escalation, daily summaries, monthly reports, and monthly report generation; web screens display supplied results/status where specified.\",\n  \"API-side production of recall traces within a time limit; the client timing requirements measure rendering after the response or from the user's request, as specified in separate requirements.\",\n  \"Supplying live temperature readings, alerts, box associations, and history through the existing logger or supplier gateway feed.\",\n  \"Importing or guaranteeing initial database contents; the web app provides opening-lot and stock entry.\",\n  \"Pricing, invoicing and payments; route stop-order optimization; manufacturer purchasing and demand forecasting; automatic driver or customer penalties; stock transfers between warehouses; logger hardware and supplier gateway implementation.\",\n  \"Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, push notifications, and background location. The product is a responsive web app; applicable notices use in-app notices or email, location uses the browser prompt, and the web app may be installable.\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A user is on the sign-in page\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned sign-in result or error message\",\n     \"when\": \"the user submits an email address and password\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A user is on the password-reset page\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned password-reset confirmation or error message\",\n     \"when\": \"the user submits an account email address\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide individual email-and-password sign-in and self-service password reset for driver, staff, and customer areas.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A System Administrator is viewing account management\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays account fields and the returned status or error message\",\n     \"when\": \"the administrator opens an account or submits account or access changes\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A user without the System Administrator role opens account management\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays an access-denied message or the account-management page is not displayed\",\n     \"when\": \"the page loads\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian web app shall provide System Administrator screens to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, staff warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\":